From 068e16270cc0c1f4bf30e9a1d9061727e77a7420 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kush J <kushisthecoolest@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:52:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] remix api: dxvk_GetInteropInfo opaque-FD interop for OpenGL
 on Linux

Exports a dedicated interop color image and two binary semaphores via
VK_KHR_external_memory_fd / VK_KHR_external_semaphore_fd, filled from
D3D9SwapchainExternal::Present's existing final-composited frame (no
dependency on Submit, which stays a 0.16-only stub). Semaphores are
binary, not timeline: GL's EXT_semaphore_fd has no wait/signal value
parameter, unlike the D3D12-fence path EXT_semaphore_win32 offers on
Windows, so dxvkDoneSemaphore_ValueToWait is informational only on
Linux.

Fixes a dead FD-export path in RtxSemaphore::createTimeline (created
with VkExportSemaphoreCreateInfo but never called vkGetSemaphoreFdKHR).

Verified on an RTX 5070 (driver 615.78.08): the mechanism itself
(export, import, synchronization, readback) is proven via two
debug-clear round trips through the real code path. A full lit scene
through the same path still renders black; root cause not yet found,
written up as an open issue for the next session.

Signed-off-by: Kush J <kushisthecoolest@gmail.com>
---
